     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>should be moved outside the output$graph &lt;- renderDygraph({...}) section. You will also probably want to extract out the code that defines uploadedFile, and make that a reactive expression. So:</div><div><br></div><div>uploadedFile &lt;- reactive({</div><div>  validate(need(input$file1, FALSE)) # This is like a better &quot;if (is.null(input$file1)) return(NULL)&quot;</div><div>  uf &lt;- read.csv(input$file1$datapath</div><div>})</div><div><br></div><div><span style=\"line-height:1.5\">observeEvent(uploadedFile(), {</span><br></div><div>  updateSelectizeInput(session, &#39;uploadChannels&#39;, choices = names(uploadedFile()))<br>})</div><div><br></div><div>output$graph &lt;- renderDygraph({</div><div>   # ... code that uses uploadedFile() ...<br>})</div><div><br></div><div><br></div></div><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div>"
    ],
